Based on the report and the animation you attached, the “space” tool currently treats an empty BPMN pool (i.e. a bpmn:Participant without any child lanes) just like any other shape and lets you stretch it vertically. However, empty pools are meant to have a fixed, dedicated height – they should not be resizable in the vertical direction at all.

To prevent that, we need to stop the space‐tool from ever including an empty pool in its “resizingShapes” when the axis is vertical. Concretely, in lib/features/space-tool/BpmnSpaceTool.js we

  1. import the helper getChildLanes( )  
  2. after we filter out TextAnnotations, also filter out any bpmn:Participant with zero child lanes if axis==='y'.  

